{"metadata":{"role":"collection","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"SnowplowEncoding"}],"title":"SnowplowEncoding","externalID":"SnowplowEncoding","symbolKind":"module"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to a Snowplow collector as self-describing events, whose schemas come from the tracking plan."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/snowplowencoding"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" makes an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") for a Snowplow pipeline in one call. It checks the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collector’s URL, the Iglu vendor and the app ID, and posts to the collector’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/com.snowplowanalytics.snowplow\/tp2"},{"type":"text","text":" endpoint with a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". It splits each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch to the limits of Snowplow’s own mobile trackers ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"): 25"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events and 40,000 bytes a request, with a larger event, of up to 150,000 bytes, in a request of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its own. A batch with no record the encoder can write, an empty one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"included, makes no request. The destination retries no response, a 5xx, 408 and 429, and drops"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and reports any other status. No trace context is sent. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves this module out;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"import it on its own."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A collector takes events from anyone who can reach it, so there is no key or secret, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination builds on every platform: an app sends to the collector directly.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import SnowplowEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let snowplow = try HTTPDestination.snowplow(","    collector: collector,  \/\/ https:\/\/collector.example.com","    vendor: \"com.example\",  \/\/ the Iglu vendor the plan is exported under","    appID: \"shop-ios\",","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: snowplow)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The factory throws "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowSetupError"},{"type":"text","text":" for a collector URL that isn’t "},{"code":"https","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", that has no host,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a user name, a query or a fragment, or that already ends in the endpoint; for a vendor Iglu"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t take; and for an empty app ID or one longer than 255 UTF-16 code units."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Schemas-from-the-tracking-plan","text":"Schemas from the tracking plan"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each event is a self-describing event: its data comes with the Iglu URI of the schema it must","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"match, and Snowplow’s pipeline validates it against that schema before loading it. The URI is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"named after the event and its version, under the vendor the destination is given:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["iglu:<vendor>\/<name>\/jsonschema\/<version>-0-0"],"syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Version N of an event is SchemaVer "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-0"},{"type":"text","text":", and events always name it. Raising an event’s version"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a breaking change, which is SchemaVer’s MODEL. The export compares each event with the newest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"schema of its version the registry holds, by what the two mean rather than their bytes, as the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plan’s own check does:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event that hasn’t changed keeps its published file, and nothing is written."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A breaking change at the same version, such as a property made required, is refused: raise the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event’s version."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A compatible change, such as an optional property added, is an ADDITION. For Iglu Server the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"export writes it as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-1"},{"text":", then ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-2"},{"text":", each listing the earlier ones in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$supersedes"},{"text":", and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Snowplow validates events naming ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-0"},{"text":" against the newest, so a release already in users’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hands keeps validating. Superseding needs Iglu Server 0.11.0 or later and Enrich 3.8.0 or later.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A static repository doesn’t support it: it would validate those events against ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-0"},{"text":" alone,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so for one the export refuses the change, and the event needs a new version.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Write the registry from the plan with ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan.writeIgluRegistry(to:vendor:registry:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"iglu <vendor> server|static <registry-directory>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" command of the tracking plan’s executable, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ","type":"text"},{"code":"export-tracking-plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"--iglu-vendor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"--iglu-registry","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Then publish it with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"igluctl","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" before the release that sends the events.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event name Iglu takes holds only ASCII letters, digits, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_"},{"type":"text","text":", and the version must be 1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or more. The encoder skips every record of an event that breaks either rule, and logs a notice for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each such event of the plan when the destination is made. The export refuses such an event too."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"What-Snowplow-receives","text":"What Snowplow receives"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each request is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"payload_data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" 1-0-4 array of events, one per record. Every event has:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"e","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"ue","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": a self-describing event, with its data in "},{"code":"ue_pr","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as JSON text;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"eid"},{"text":", the record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dtm"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ttm"},{"type":"text","text":", the record’s timestamp in milliseconds, so Snowplow’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"derived_tstamp"},{"type":"text","text":" is when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the event was tracked;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"aid"},{"type":"text","text":", the app ID; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":", the platform; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tv"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":"; and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0.0.0.0"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No ","type":"text"},{"code":"stm","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is sent: a retried request sends the same body again, so a sent time would be the first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attempt’s, and Snowplow would move the event later by however long the retries took.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The standard context, when the record has it, goes in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"co"},{"text":" as Snowplow’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mobile_context"},{"text":" 1-0-3","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(the operating system, Apple as the manufacturer, the device model, the network type and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"language) and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application"},{"text":" 1-0-0 (the app’s version and build). The platform is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mob"},{"text":" for a phone,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pad, watch or Vision Pro, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tv"},{"text":" for an Apple TV, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pc"},{"text":" for a Mac and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app"},{"text":" for a record with no device.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Only-the-session-identifies-a-record","text":"Only the session identifies a record"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s session, from the sessions enricher, is its "},{"code":"sid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", Snowplow’s "},{"code":"domain_sessionid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing else identifies it. No "},{"code":"duid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"uid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"nuid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"tnuid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is sent, no "},{"code":"client_session","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entity (its "},{"code":"userId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lasts across sessions), and no IDFV, IDFA or other device identifier. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record’s vendor identifier and trace context aren’t sent either. A record with no session, from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracker without the sessions enricher, is sent without a "},{"code":"sid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; a record a store recovered after a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relaunch keeps its session and its "},{"code":"sid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Snowplow’s mobile data models"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"read a session from the "},{"code":"client_session","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" entity, so set the unified package’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"snowplow__session_identifiers","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"code":"[{\"schema\": \"atomic\", \"field\": \"domain_sessionid\"}]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for these"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The collector would give each device an identifier of its own: it sets an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sp"},{"type":"text","text":" cookie, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps and sends back, and records the request’s IP address. Every request carries"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SP-Anonymous: *"},{"type":"text","text":", so the collector sets and reads no cookie, records "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"network_userid"},{"type":"text","text":" as all"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"zeros, and records no IP address or forwarding header fields."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Records-left-out","text":"Records left out"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t "},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose event name Iglu doesn’t take, or whose version is below 1;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose timestamp falls outside the years 0 to 9999, which Snowplow’s enrichment fails;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose JSON is over 150,000 bytes, which the smallest of a pipeline’s streams, SQS’s 192 kB,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"might not take with the request around it."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The destination reports each as "},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"What-the-collector-doesnt-report","text":"What the collector doesn’t report"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The collector answers 200 to every request it can read and validates nothing. Snowplow checks the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events later, in enrichment. An event whose data its schema rejects, whose schema the pipeline’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Iglu resolver can’t find, or that is larger than the pipeline’s stream takes, becomes a failed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event: it is kept apart and never reaches the warehouse, though the destination counted it as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered. Publish each schema before the release that sends it, and watch the pipeline’s failed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events after a change to the plan. Snowplow’s resolver caches schemas, for 10 minutes by default,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so a schema published after the first event that names it can still be missed for that long.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Snowplow doesn’t remove duplicates as events arrive. A record is sent more than once when a request","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is retried after the collector stored it but the answer was lost, when a delivery sends a cancelled","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batch again, and when a store redelivers records after a relaunch. Each copy keeps its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"eid"},{"text":", so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Snowplow’s data models, which deduplicate on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event_id"},{"text":", count it once.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what Snowplow receives, and why, in more detail."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowSetupError"],"title":"Sending to Snowplow","anchor":"Sending-to-Snowplow"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder"],"title":"Encoding batches","anchor":"Encoding-batches"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError"],"title":"Records left out","anchor":"Records-left-out"}],"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"abstract":[{"text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"HTTPDestinations","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/choosingdestinations":{"title":"Choosing Destinations","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Choosing Destinations"}],"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding/SnowplowBatchEncoder/init(vendor:appID:plan:limit:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"An encoder of the events ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" describes, whose schemas are under ","type":"text"},{"code":"vendor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", sent as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"app ","type":"text"},{"code":"appID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", splitting each batch to ","type":"text"},{"code":"limit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding\/snowplowbatchencoder\/init(vendor:appid:plan:limit:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"vendor","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"appID","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"plan","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TrackingPlan","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"limit","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchLimit","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"SnowplowSetupError","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SnowplowEncoding0A10SetupErrorO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/init(vendor:appID:plan:limit:)","title":"init(vendor:appID:plan:limit:)"},"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding/SnowplowBatchEncoder":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of Snowplow’s tracker protocol, so an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can send events to a Snowplow collector’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/com.snowplowanalytics.snowplow\/tp2"},{"type":"text","text":", as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"self-describing events whose schemas are the tracking plan’s."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SnowplowBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding\/snowplowbatchencoder","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SnowplowBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder","title":"SnowplowBatchEncoder"},"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding/SnowplowSetupError":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SnowplowSetupError","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"SnowplowSetupError","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SnowplowSetupError","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/init(vendor:appID:plan:limit:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" couldn’t be made."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowSetupError","url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding\/snowplowsetuperror"},"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:tra